Troubleshooting Tips
Elasticsearch won't start:

Check JVM heap size matches available RAM
Verify disk space: df -h
Review logs: sudo journalctl -u elasticsearch -n 50
No logs appearing in Kibana:

Verify Logstash is processing: sudo systemctl status logstash
Check Filebeat connection: sudo filebeat test output
Confirm log files exist and are readable
Python script errors:

Ensure virtual environment is activated
Verify Elasticsearch connection: curl localhost:9200
Check file permissions on log files
Review script logs for specific error messages
Kibana dashboard shows no data:

Verify index pattern matches indexed data
Check time range filter (expand to last 7 days)
Confirm logs are being indexed: curl localhost:9200/_cat/indices?v
Conclusion
This lab provided hands-on experience building a complete SIEM solution using the ELK Stack and Wazuh. You learned to install and configure distributed logging infrastructure, integrate security monitoring tools, automate log processing with Python, and visualize security events through custom dashboards.

Key takeaways:

ELK Stack provides powerful log aggregation and analysis capabilities
Wazuh enhances security monitoring with HIDS functionality
Automation scripts improve efficiency and enable real-time monitoring
Visualization helps identify security patterns and anomalies
Continue exploring by adding more log sources, creating advanced queries, and developing custom alerting rules based on security events.
